   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Along The Road**: back after 52 archived shows (618 days) [5]\n- **Streamline Cannonball**: back after 44 archived shows (597 days) [5]\n- **Morning Light**: rare: 14 archived performances [5]\n- **Planet Caravan**: back after 75 archived shows (716 days) [5]\n- **Believe**: back after 73 archived shows (710 days); rare: 9 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2021-10-17.matrix.stearns.flac16** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 22 songs; 136 min [1]\n- **billystrings2021-10-17.dpa4011**: source not stated; 22 songs; 136 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]\n- **billystrings2021-10-17**: source not stated; 22 songs; 132 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Taping position was the taper section (BOB) on the floor, row D, eight feet high, about 80 feet from the stage [2]\n- Reviewer says the taper recorded all four nights of the Denver run [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2021-10-17.matrix.stearns.flac16**: taped by Ryan Stearns; transferred by Ryan Stearns; source: AKG CK-61 ULS (NOS) + AKG CK-63 ULS (DIN) > Nbob actives > Naiant PFA's > Sound Devices MixPre 6 II @ 24bit/48kHz Location: OTS/BOB/DFC 8ft up [1]. Also: Transfer: four-channel mix, EQ, gain and fades in WaveLab 6, dithered to 16bit/48kHz with Apogee UV22HR, tracked in CDWave, FLAC6 via Traders Little Helper [1]\n- **billystrings2021-10-17.dpa4011**: taped by Rob O'Brien; transferred by Rob O'Brien; source: DPA 4011(DIN) > Sound Devices MixPre-6 II(24/96) [2]. Also: Taped with DPA 4011 (DIN) mics into a Sound Devices MixPre-6 II at 24/96, then edited in Wave Lab 6.1 and tracked in CD Wave [2]\n- **billystrings2021-10-17**: taped by Brain; transferred by Brain; source: Schoeps CMC6/MK4> Sound Devices MixPre-6 [3]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by @BillybaseDotNet: [Billy Strings The Mission Ballroom - BillyBase](https://billybase.net/venue/mission-ballroom/) [6]\n- Fan art by @BillybaseDotNet: [Billy Strings The Mission Ballroom - BillyBase](https://billybase.net/venue/mission-ballroom/) [7]",
